{"lines":[{"h":0.008720930389296444,"c":0.30000001192092896,"x":0.7716049391467531,"w":0.069958845774332645,"y":0.046511627815394085,"t":"1718867188"},{"w":0.29012346903483077,"x":0.1008230390430009,"y":0.097383720794351092,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"w":0.77180801391601572,"x":0.10277500108998121,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","y":0.12946051787776691,"h":0.019794942633423296,"c":1},{"h":0.016012083936495891,"t":"Passage 2 below.","y":0.14807870784925958,"x":0.10058752590965729,"w":0.16104527791341144,"c":1},{"x":0.10082304530196955,"y":0.38662790675017877,"w":0.016460905075073237,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"B"},{"w":0.016460905075073237,"c":1,"x":0.10082304530196955,"y":0.5523255811687835,"t":"C","h":0.013081395583944611},{"x":0.22831219529096358,"w":0.53105326334635417,"c":1,"h":0.024515685540908105,"t":"Does education fuel economic growth?","y":0.181645091772071},{"w":0.66872426350911462,"y":0.22084805636488825,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.14609054303284541,"t":"Over the last decade, a huge database about the lives of southwest German villagers"},{"h":0.014553715960858749,"y":0.23691860449978341,"w":0.69958847045898442,"t":"between 1600 and 1900 has been compiled by a team led by Professor Sheilagh Ogilvie","x":0.14609053870936728,"c":1},{"y":0.25436046498334197,"c":1,"t":"at Cambridge University's Faculty of Economics. It includes court records, guild ledgers,","x":0.14609052828060973,"w":0.70987655639648439,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"h":0.014546867815428799,"c":1,"x":0.14609054178444514,"w":0.732510274251302,"t":"parish registers, village censuses, tax lists and - the most recent addition - 9,000 handwritten","y":0.2717903416152827},{"x":0.14398236071716383,"y":0.286320033216517,"t":"inventories listing over a million personal possessions belonging to ordinary women and","w":0.70585449218749996,"c":1,"h":0.01647423630749234},{"t":"men across three centuries. Ogilvie, who discovered the inventories in the archives of two","x":0.14602100559038869,"w":0.71411941528320311,"c":1,"y":0.30266984394271423,"h":0.016847988461156316},{"y":0.32122093011309749,"t":"German communities 30 years ago, believes they may hold the answer to a conundrum that","x":0.14609052545483811,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"w":0.72839508056640623},{"t":"has long puzzled economists: the lack of evidence for a causal link between education and a","x":0.14397771314497657,"c":1,"y":0.33459397415353265,"w":0.73467391967773443,"h":0.018751698191792121},{"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1,"w":0.22633745829264321,"y":0.35453474698644016,"x":0.14403291687652872,"t":"country's economic growth."},{"y":0.38662790682918668,"x":0.14403291543797081,"w":0.65226338704427089,"c":1,"t":"As Ogilvie explains, 'Education helps us to work more productively, invent better","h":0.01598837238037687},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.40253239095850268,"w":0.70781890869140618,"t":"technology, and earn more... surely it must be critical for economic growth? But, if you","c":1,"x":0.1419753195696408},{"x":0.14197531481453723,"w":0.68106994628906259,"y":0.42005813938868508,"t":"look back through history, there's no evidence that having a high literacy rate made a","h":0.016043156420524673,"c":1},{"w":0.72016459147135414,"h":0.01744185965530165,"x":0.14403292324580452,"t":"country industrialise earlier: Between 1600 and 1900, England had only mediocre literacy","c":1,"y":0.43459302344269801},{"c":1,"w":0.67901234944661459,"t":"rates by European standards, yet its economy grew fast and it was the first country to","x":0.14197530664323721,"y":0.45347467623035498,"h":0.014548579711374909},{"y":0.46937573600113291,"t":"industrialise. During this period, Germany and Scandinavia had excellent literacy rates, but","w":0.72839508056640623,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.14403291228612944,"c":1},{"t":"their economies grew slowly and they industrialised late. 'Modern cross-country analyses","x":0.14403291416762631,"y":0.48691860451834523,"w":0.71604939778645837,"c":1,"h":0.014553715960858638},{"w":0.71193415323893228,"t":"have also struggled to find evidence that education causes economic growth, even though","y":0.50290697659507111,"c":1,"x":0.1440329232965496,"h":0.015988372380376759},{"c":1,"t":"there is plenty of evidence that growth increases education,' she adds.","x":0.14403292530331707,"w":0.5576131693522135,"y":0.51737338036459746,"h":0.017510339986309131},{"c":1,"y":0.55232558124857345,"t":"In the handwritten inventories that Ogilvie is analysing are the belongings of women and","x":0.1419753019437969,"w":0.70987655639648439,"h":0.015990084276322869},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.56976744172721672,"c":1,"t":"men at marriage, remarriage and death. From badger skins to Bibles, sewing machines to","x":0.14403292328659925,"w":0.71193415323893239},{"w":0.73268086751302075,"x":0.14394590908220464,"t":"scarlet bodices - the villagers' entire worldly goods are included. Inventories of agricultural","h":0.019716916572921406,"c":1,"y":0.58339689238915515},{"y":0.60306242664258802,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"t":"equipment and craft tools reveal economic activities; ownership of books and education-","w":0.70781890869140629,"x":0.14403293239717699},{"x":0.14197533194500692,"w":0.70987650553385417,"h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1,"t":"related objects like pens and slates suggests how people learned. In addition, the tax lists","y":0.61918604676971312},{"t":"included in the database record the value of farms, workshops, assets and debts; signatures","y":0.63662790684363169,"w":0.72427983601888024,"x":0.14403292137228599,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"y":0.64958775020847637,"h":0.019140164899882239,"t":"and people's estimates of their age indicate literacy and numeracy levels; and court records","x":0.14403292917853644,"c":1,"w":0.72633743286132812},{"t":"reveal obstacles (such as the activities of the guilds*) that stifled industry.","h":0.016024324441826665,"c":1,"x":0.14197531174992881,"y":0.66860465101310318,"w":0.59053497314453118},{"y":0.70200235586647608,"c":1,"h":0.016020900088288936,"x":0.14609053454819521,"t":"Previous studies usually had just one way of linking education with economic growth - the","w":0.72427983601888024},{"y":0.71937573601390681,"w":0.69753087361653643,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.14403291700716608,"t":"presence of schools and printing presses, perhaps, or school enrolment, or the ability to","c":1},{"h":0.016007204359074767,"y":0.73546511611635923,"w":0.70987655639648439,"t":"sign names. According to Ogilvie, the database provides multiple indicators for the same","c":1,"x":0.14403291474463459},{"h":0.016039886519541025,"y":0.75132691075657143,"t":"individuals, making it possible to analyse links between literacy, numeracy, wealth, and","w":0.69352091471354171,"c":1,"x":0.14603172256703129},{"w":0.53722442626953126,"x":0.14598666666681401,"y":0.7672147976140079,"c":1,"h":0.017744505222891171,"t":"industriousness, for individual women and men over the long term."},{"y":0.84590985094499882,"h":0.013234339557912755,"c":1,"w":0.65029881795247402,"t":"* guild: an association of artisans or merchants which oversees the practice of their craft or trade in a particular area","x":0.10077264813036749},{"t":"85","c":1,"x":0.8580246914705375,"w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.86773255796252025},{"c":1,"x":0.66991655033568553,"w":0.30612678527832038,"h":0.03375352650564889,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","y":0.95314993796778535}],"h":3395,"w":2400}